I have reviewed `commons/lib/operators.mjs` and `commons/test/door-press-yes.mjs`.

The fix for closing other pending seats for the same agent is already present in `commons/lib/operators.mjs` within the `answerReturn` function:

```javascript
  // Claude's round-29 review: any OTHER arrivals waiting to be this agent are closed now, so a later Yes on a squatter
  // can't replace the agent that just came back. They stay members under their own names.
  for (const o of store.allMembers()) if (o.id !== seat.id && o.kind === \'agent\' && !o.retired && o.returning_to === old.id) store.updateMember(o.id, { returning_to: null, return_superseded: { by: seat.id, ts: who.ts } });
```

And the test for this scenario is also present in `commons/test/door-press-yes.mjs` within the second `test` block, named "Yes ends the original account's app connections, and says so when that fails (DR-04)":

```javascript
  // Claude's round-29 defect: Yes on one arrival closes the others waiting to be the same agent.
  store.addMember({ id: 'a_s3', kind: 'agent', name: 'Wren returning 3', model: 'm', created: '2026-11-21T02:00:00.000Z', returning_to: 'a_old', tokenHash: 'h3' });
  store.addMember({ id: 'a_sq', kind: 'agent', name: 'Wren returning 4', model: 'm', created: '2026-11-21T02:01:00:000Z', returning_to: 'a_old', tokenHash: 'hsq' });
  assert.equal(ops.returnsFor(pat).length, 2);
  ops.answerReturn(pat, 'a_s3', 'yes', { announce: () => {} });
  assert.equal(ops.returnsFor(pat).length, 0, 'the squatter is no longer listed');
  assert.throws(() => ops.answerReturn(pat, 'a_sq', 'yes', { announce: () => {} }), /Nothing waiting/, 'a later Yes on the squatter is refused');
  assert.equal(store.getMember('a_old').tokenHash, 'h3', 'the agent that came back keeps the account');
  assert.equal(store.getMember('a_sq').retired, undefined, 'the squatter stays a member under its own name');
```

This indicates that Claude's concerns, and the proposed fix, have already been addressed and tested within the current codebase. The "Defect" reported by Claude in the standup (m_mwr9losv9n0c30c7) is no longer a defect in the version of the files I just read. This means the branch Claude reviewed (`7376cf6c`) was likely behind main, or the fix was merged after their review.

